| `orthogonal()` | 0.06250 | 1.0000 | -0.75 | 4.00 |

Orthogonal [256, 128]: largest |QᵀQ − I| = 2.4e-15. Truncated-normal factor √(1 − 4φ(2)/(2Φ(2) − 1)) = 0.87962566; gains: tanh 1.6667, relu 1.4142, leaky_relu(0.2) 1.3868, selu 0.75.
// result_end

The first table is the original example's lifecycle. A declared `Tensor` has no value, and reading it throws. After assignment, `add_` and `copy_` change the
buffer that both `w` and its alias share. A row update rebuilds the matrix from a slice of itself and copies it back in. The clone in a second `ParameterStore` changes while the
original stays at \([[20,30],[-1,-2]]\). The gradient of \(\sum v^2\) at \(v=(11,12,13)\) is \(2v=(22,24,26)\). Two generators seeded with 123 draw the same numbers.

In the second table every initialiser's sample standard deviation is within 0.6% of its target, and every sample mean is within 2.2 standard errors of zero. The other
column shows each distribution's shape. Uniform draws reach at most \(\sqrt3=1.73\) target standard deviations. Truncated normals stop at \(2/0.8796=2.27\), the two-sigma truncation
expressed in units of the narrower standard deviation. Normals run to about 4 to 5. `truncated_normal(0.02)` has a target of \(0.02\times0.8796=0.0176\), not 0.02, while
`variance_scaling(1, FanIn, TruncatedNormal)` hits \(1/\sqrt{256}\) because it applies the correction. The orthogonal matrix's columns are orthonormal to \(2.4\times10^{-15}\). That
forces its mean square to be exactly \(128/(256\cdot128)=1/256\), which is why its ratio is 1.0000.

> Checking the theory

>> Signals and gradients through 50 layers

`nn::init::signal_propagation` pushes a batch of 512 standard-normal inputs through a fresh bias-free network and records the RMS of each layer's pre-activations, and of
the gradients for a loss \(\sum\text{output}\odot r\) with random \(r\). The networks below have 50 layers of width 256 and normal weights with variance \(s/256\). The mean-field
predictions come from the recursion above, with the tanh expectations computed by quadrature.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/variables_initializers_signal.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace init = dm::nn::init;
using nn::Tensor;

// E[phi(sqrt(q) Z)^2] for Z ~ N(0, 1), by the trapezoid rule on [-10, 10].
template <class Phi> double second_moment(double q, Phi phi) {
  const int m = 4000;
  const double h = 20.0 / m;
  double s = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) {
    const double z = -10 + i * h, f = phi(std::sqrt(q) * z);
    s += (i == 0 || i == m ? 0.5 : 1.0) * f * f * std::exp(-0.5 * z * z);
  }
  return s * h / std::sqrt(2 * std::numbers::pi);
}

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::int64_t width = 256, depth = 50, batch = 512;
  const std::vector<std::int64_t> widths(depth + 1, width);
  nn::Generator gen(4);
  const auto relu = [](const Tensor& x) { return nn::relu(x); };
  const auto tanh_ = [](const Tensor& x) { return nn::tanh(x); };
  struct Curve { std::string label; double scale; bool is_relu; std::vector<double> measured, predicted, backward; };
  std::vector<Curve> curves = {{"ReLU, scale 1.6", 1.6, true}, {"ReLU, scale 1.8", 1.8, true}, {"ReLU, scale 2 (He)", 2.0, true},
                               {"ReLU, scale 2.2", 2.2, true}, {"ReLU, scale 2.4", 2.4, true},
                               {"tanh, scale 1 (LeCun)", 1.0, false}, {"tanh, scale 25/9 (gain 5/3)", 25.0 / 9, false}, {"tanh, scale 4", 4.0, false}};
  std::print("| network | forward RMS, layer 1 | layer 10 | layer 50 | mean-field layer 50 | gradient RMS, layer 1 / layer 50 | mean-field gradient ratio |\n");
  std::print("| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (auto& c : curves) {
    const auto sp = init::signal_propagation(widths, init::variance_scaling(c.scale, init::FanMode::FanIn, init::Distribution::Normal),
                                             c.is_relu ? std::function<Tensor(const Tensor&)>(relu) : std::function<Tensor(const Tensor&)>(tanh_), batch, gen);
    c.measured = sp.forward_rms, c.backward = sp.backward_rms;
    // Mean field: q_1 = scale (unit-variance inputs), q_{l+1} = scale E[phi(z_l)^2].
    // Gradients: Var(g_{l-1}) = scale E[phi'(z_{l-1})^2] Var(g_l), so the ratio from layer 50 back to layer 1 is the
    // square root of the product of those factors over layers 1..49.
    double q = c.scale, log_chi = 0;
    for (std::int64_t l = 0; l < depth; ++l) {
      c.predicted.push_back(std::sqrt(q));
      if (l < depth - 1)
        log_chi += std::log(c.scale * (c.is_relu ? 0.5 : second_moment(q, [](double z) { return 1.0 / (std::cosh(z) * std::cosh(z)); })));
      q = c.scale * (c.is_relu ? 0.5 * q : second_moment(q, [](double z) { return std::tanh(z); }));
    }
    std::print("| {} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} | {:.3g} |\n", c.label, c.measured[0], c.measured[9], c.measured[49], c.predicted[49],
               c.backward.front() / c.backward.back(), std::exp(0.5 * log_chi));
  }
  // The tanh fixed points q* = scale E[tanh(sqrt(q*) Z)^2], by iteration.
  for (double s : {25.0 / 9, 4.0}) {
    double q = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i < 2000; ++i) q = s * second_moment(q, [](double z) { return std::tanh(z); });
    std::print("\nTanh fixed point for scale {:.3f}: RMS √q* = {:.4f}.", s, std::sqrt(q));
  }
  std::print("\n");

  const dm::graphics::RGB cols[] = {{147, 51, 234}, {8, 145, 178}, {37, 99, 235}, {234, 88, 12}, {220, 38, 38}};
  auto panel = [&](bool is_relu, const std::string& title, double lo, double hi) {
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    int k = 0;
    for (const auto& c : curves) {
      if (c.is_relu != is_relu) continue;
      std::vector<double> layer, m, pr;
      for (std::int64_t l = 0; l < depth; ++l) layer.push_back(double(l + 1)), m.push_back(std::log10(c.measured[l])), pr.push_back(std::log10(c.predicted[l]));
      const auto col = cols[is_relu ? k : (k == 0 ? 0 : k == 1 ? 2 : 4)];
      p.lines(layer, pr, "", dm::graphics::RGB{col.r, col.g, col.b, 0.35}, 5.0);
      p.lines(layer, m, c.label.substr(c.label.find(", ") + 2), col, 1.8);
      ++k;
    }
    p.x_limits(0, 52).y_limits(lo, hi).title(title).x_label("layer").y_label("log10 RMS of pre-activations");
    return p;
  };
  auto fig = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  fig.add(panel(true, "ReLU, width 256", -3, 5));
  fig.add(panel(false, "tanh, width 256", -1.5, 1));
  fig.size(1100, 460).fit_panels();
  fig.save("build/variables_initializers_signal.svg");
}
```
